# interencdec — Cryptoghraphy
Difficulty: easy
Tools: linux "cat", online decoder (cyberchef)

What I was given: A file with no file extension. Little to no intructions
What worked: Decoding the file twice and using further decipher it using ceaser cipcher
Steps: 
  1. Download the file
  2. Open terminal 
  3. use "cat" to view the file content
  4. Identify the format of the given text (base64 because of the appended "==")
  5. Decode the text for the first time
  6. Take the previous decoded message and decode it further (only decode the text between the ' symbol)
  7. Use caeser cipher to decipher it and obtain the flag (ROT -7) 
Things I learned: 
  1. "cat" in linux can be used to view the text of weird files. 
  2. Be aware that cipher and encoding can be stacked with one another.
